 | `framework/kernel/xelex/mt6789/0902-SableOS-no-phantom-Q25-keys-after-the-screen-wakes.patch` | `2a873a3511ee0eeead1442e60145093192a4535d` + 0201, 0202, 0901 | Keyboard: no phantom keys after the screen wakes. `bbqX0kbd`'s screen-off path cut the keyboard's power (or parked its IRQ) without releasing held keys, so a key or trackpad click down at that moment never got its release and Android repeated it until another key went down; on wake the IRQ came back before the controller's FIFO and `REG_INT` were cleared, and the trackpad's arrow accumulators kept pre-sleep values. Screen off now flushes key work and releases every held key; screen on drains the FIFO, clears `REG_INT` and resets the trackpad state before enabling the IRQ. Num lock is kept. The driver is the same blob on lineage-23.2 and lineage-24.0. Uncompiled; not run on hardware. |
 | `framework/kernel/xelex/mt6789/0903-SableOS-double-tap-to-wake-on-the-Q25-touch-panel.patch` | `2a873a3511ee0eeead1442e60145093192a4535d` + 0201, 0202, 0901, 0902 | Double-tap to wake: the open `synaptics_dsx` touch driver the Q25 build uses gets a `wake_gesture` module parameter (off by default). When the display powers down with it on (MediaTek's `mtk_disp_notifier`), F12 goes to wakeup-gesture report mode with double tap enabled, its interrupt becomes a wake source and system suspend leaves the sensor awake; a double tap reports `KEY_WAKEUP`, and the display powering up puts F12 back in continuous mode. Touches only `synaptics_dsx_core.c`, so it applies in any order with the earlier kernel patches. Works only if the panel firmware has the F12 wakeup gesture (the driver skips it otherwise) and the panel keeps power with the display off. Uncompiled; not run on hardware. |
 | `framework/device/xelex/Q25/1501-SableOS-type-on-the-Q25-currency-key.patch` | `1f4e295b5b972bd5e5ea0ec01f8a87154973b464` | $ key: `Q25_keyboard.kcm` gets a `key GRAVE` entry (label, base, Shift and Caps Lock '$'). The keyboard sends scan code 41 (GRAVE) for its printed $ key and the kcm had no entry, so keyboards typed '`' or nothing. Replaces the remapping part of aesophor/q25-gboard-patch without its Alt and A remaps (they would break Sable's Alt shortcuts). Not run on hardware. |
+| `framework/device/xelex/Q25/1502-SableOS-Space-T-and-B-scroll-in-any-app.patch` | `1f4e295b5b972bd5e5ea0ec01f8a87154973b464` + 1501 | System-wide key scrolling (2.0 plan): `Q25_keyboard.kcm` gives plain Space and Shift+Space the fallback keys PAGE_DOWN and PAGE_UP, and plain T and B MOVE_HOME and MOVE_END. Android's input dispatcher sends a keychar map fallback only when the app leaves the key unhandled, so text fields and app shortcuts keep the key; lists, scroll views and web pages then page and jump. Sable apps keep their own SableListKeys handling. |
 | `framework/device/xelex/mt6789-common/1502-SableOS-let-Settings-drive-the-Q25-keyboard-firmware.patch` | `fd308035cdbf58f5de46515fb0a0e97fe5453980` (lineage-24.0; the Q25 sepolicy moved to mt6789-common) | Keyboard firmware: labels `/proc/firmware_upgrade` `proc_sable_kbd_fw` (it was generic `proc`, root only) and lets `system_app` read and write it, for Settings 1501. Not compiled. |
 | `framework/device/xelex/mt6789-common/1503-SableOS-let-init-set-the-Q25-trackpad-mode.patch` | `fd308035cdbf58f5de46515fb0a0e97fe5453980` + 1502 | Trackpad mode: labels `/proc/q20_switch_key_mouse` `proc_sable_trackpad` (mode 0777 but generic `proc`, root only, as seen on 2026-11-05) and lets init write it and `system_app` only check it exists, for Settings 1605 and `sable-trackpad.rc`. Not compiled. |
 | `framework/frameworks/base/0301-SableOS-keyboard-notification-commands-in-the-shade.patch` | `f4ed08a03b518772ba77c3c0a1b4185fa1712c9b` | KF-A: contextual single-key commands on a focused notification row (Space, R, D, Z, M, C, H); text input always wins. H opens Sable Start's Hub page (`org.sableos.start.action.SHOW_HUB`) on the Messages tab for messages and mail, Calls for calls, else All (pure `notification/sable/SableHubRoute.java`, host-tested). New router, command glue and a router unit test; three small hooks in `ExpandableNotificationRow`. |
